{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"agent_message","text":"\n\nNow I have a clear picture. Three failures, each with a distinct root cause:\n\n1. **API test**: `create_entry` calls `session.commit()` inside a `session_factory.begin()` block, closing the transaction prematurely.\n2. **Worker test**: `settle_entry` commits the intermediate \"processing\" status before the error, so the status isn't rolled back.\n3. **Admin CLI test**: `plan_batch` commits even on `dry_run=True`, persisting the \"queued\" status.\n\nThe fix: move `commit()` out of repository helpers, convert queries to SQLAlchemy 2.x `select()`, and add proper transaction boundaries with rollback in the API, worker, and admin CLI.\n\n"}}
